  "scenario": {
    "name": "ladder-gpu-n",
    "description": "Task 5.2 GPU rungs on the Runpod A40 (D37, D38): YOLO11n with PyTorch FP32 on CUDA (the GPU baseline), ONNX Runtime FP32 with the CUDA provider, TensorRT FP16 (engine from the FP16 export) and TensorRT INT8 (engine from the symmetric Q/DQ model, calibration set v1, head decode in FP32), each in its own process. Model-only: detect_batch (letterbox, forward, NMS; pre- and post-processing on the CPU, as the worker runs them) on decoded data-mini frames (1280x720, as loadgen sends them) at batch sizes 1, 4 and 8, rotated step order. After the speed runs every step is scored on the detection subset and the pairs below are compared (paired bootstrap; D32 verdict for INT8 against TensorRT FP16).\n",
